	<complexType name="OftpCommunicationSetupType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>Each setup file shall contain the complete information of the station(s). A new file replaces the previous settings completely. </documentation>
		</annotation>
		<sequence>
			<element name="StationInformation" type="ocs:StationInfoType" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1"/>
			<element name="InboundCommunicationSettings" type="ocs:InboundCommunicationSettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1"/>
			<element name="OutboundCommunicationSettings" type="ocs:OutboundCommunicationSettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1"/>
			<element name="CipherSetting" type="ocs:CipherSettingType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1"/>
			<element name="SessionSettings" type="ocs:SessionSettingsType" maxOccurs="1"/>
			<element name="OutboundFileSettings" type="ocs:OutboundFileSettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
  				Information about security settings on file level for
  				outgoing files (i.e. files being sent by the station
  				described in this document).

  				If file signature is set to be supported and/or
  				required, the corresponding certificate being used
  				must be provided.
  			</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="InboundFileSettings" type="ocs:InboundFileSettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
  				Information about security settings on file level for
  				incoming files (i.e. files being received by the
  				station described in this document).

  				If file encryption is set to be supported and/or
  				required, the corresponding certificate being used
  				must be provided. If EERP signature is set to be
  				supported and/or required, the corresponding
  				certificate being used must be provided.
  			</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="OutboundDsnList" type="ocs:DsnPatternListType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>List of SFIDDSN pattern that are send out from this SubStation.
It is not needed to list the build in DSNs for OFTP2 certificate exchange (ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_REQUEST, ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_DELIVER, ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_REPLACE) and for setup exchange (OFTPCOMMUNICATIONSETUP), because they should generally be present in every OFTP2 system.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="InboundDsnList" type="ocs:DsnPatternListType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>List of SFIDDSN pattern that will be accepted from this SubStation.
It is not needed to list the build in DSNs for OFTP2 certificate exchange (ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_REQUEST, ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_DELIVER, ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_REPLACE) and for setup exchange (OFTPCOMMUNICATIONSETUP), because they should generally be present in every OFTP2 system.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="SubStations" type="ocs:SubStationsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1"/>
			<element name="Certificates" type="ocs:CertificatesType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1"/>
		</sequence>
		<attribute name="version" use="required">
			<annotation>
				<documentation>Version of the schema specification</documentation>
			</annotation>
			<simpleType>
				<restriction base="string">
					<enumeration value="1.2"/>
				</restriction>
			</simpleType>
		</attribute>
		<attribute name="docid" use="required">
			<annotation>
				<documentation>Unique ID of the document</documentation>
			</annotation>
			<simpleType>
				<restriction base="ocs:UUID"/>
			</simpleType>
		</attribute>
		<attribute name="docdate" type="ocs:dateTimeTZ" use="required">
			<annotation>
				<documentation>Creation date and time of this particular document</documentation>
				<documentation source="Remark">It is recommended to check that the date/time of a setup file intended to be imported into a system is more recent as the previously imported information.</documentation>
			</annotation>
		</attribute>
		<attribute name="validfrom" use="required">
			<annotation>
				<documentation>The date and time these settings should take effect.</documentation>
			</annotation>
			<simpleType>
				<restriction base="ocs:dateTimeTZ"/>
			</simpleType>
		</attribute>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="OutboundCommunicationSettingsType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>Network settings for outbound communication (connections from the station described in this document)</documentation>
		</annotation>
		<sequence>
			<element name="OutboundConnectionSettings" type="ocs:OutboundConnectionSettingType" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="OutboundConnectionSettingType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>Network connection settings for a particular connection-type</documentation>
		</annotation>
		<complexContent>
			<extension base="ocs:ConnectionSettingType">
				<sequence>
					<element name="OutboundIP" type="string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<annotation>
							<documentation>An IP-address to be expected when this server is performing outbound network connections</documentation>
						</annotation>
					</element>
					<element name="TLSClientAuth" type="ocs:SupportInfoType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
						<annotation>
							<documentation>
Information if TLS client authentication is supported and/or required when setting up TLS connections.

If TLS client authentication is set to be supported and/or required, the used certificate must be provided.
              </documentation>
						</annotation>
					</element>
				</sequence>
			</extension>
		</complexContent>
	</complexType>
	<simpleType name="ProtocolReleaseLevelType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>Release version of the OFTP protocol</documentation>
		</annotation>
		<restriction base="string">
			<minLength value="1"/>
			<enumeration value="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation source="Name">OFTP V1.2</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
			<enumeration value="2">
				<annotation>
					<documentation source="Name">OFTP V1.3</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
			<enumeration value="4">
				<annotation>
					<documentation source="Name">OFTP V1.4</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
			<enumeration value="5">
				<annotation>
					<documentation source="Name">OFTP V2.0</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
		</restriction>
	</simpleType>
	<complexType name="SessionSettingsType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>Settings for session setup</documentation>
		</annotation>
		<sequence>
			<element name="OdetteIDCodeSSID" type="ocs:OdetteIDType" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>The Odette ID of this station being used during session setup (SSID). This can be a gateway as well.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="MinimumProtocolReleaseLevel" type="ocs:ProtocolReleaseLevelType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
The minimum protocol release level this station
                        expects
          </documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="MaximumProtocolReleaseLevel" type="ocs:ProtocolReleaseLevelType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
The maximum protocol release level this station
                        supports
          </documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="Password" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
This element is not part of the base information
                        document, provided by a repository system but
                        only intended for direct exchange between peers.
          </documentation>
				</annotation>
				<simpleType>
					<restriction base="string">
						<minLength value="0"/>
						<maxLength value="8"/>
					</restriction>
				</simpleType>
			</element>
			<element name="SecureAuthentication" type="ocs:SupportInfoType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
Information if this station supports and/or
                        requires Secure Authentication.
          </documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="StationInfoType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>Main information about the station this document describes</documentation>
		</annotation>
		<sequence>
			<element name="DUNS" type="string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>The DUNS identifier if available</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="Name" type="string" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>The name of the station</documentation>
					<documentation source="Example">ACME Inc. -EDI</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="CompanyInfo" type="ocs:CompanyInfoType" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation/>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="IssuerIDCode" type="ocs:OdetteIDType" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>The Odette ID of the issuer of this file. </documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="InfoDocumentURL" type="anyURI" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Additional information about this station, e.g. naming schemes for virtual filenames, etc.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="Contacts" type="ocs:ContactsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation/>
				</annotation>
			</element>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="SubStationInfoType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>Information about a particular sub station</documentation>
		</annotation>
		<sequence>
			<element name="Name" type="string" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
  				A describing name of the sub station
  			</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="OdetteIDCodeSFID" type="ocs:OdetteIDType" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
  				The Odette ID of this sub station being used during
  				file exchange (SFID)
  			</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="OutboundFileSettings" type="ocs:OutboundFileSettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
  				File security settings for outbound files if they
  				differ from the main settings
  			</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="InboundFileSettings" type="ocs:InboundFileSettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
  				File security settings for inbound files if they
  				differ from the main settings
  			</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="OutboundDsnList" type="ocs:DsnPatternListType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>List of SFIDDSN pattern that are send out from the system.
It is not needed to list the build in DSNs for OFTP2 certificate exchange (ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_REQUEST, ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_DELIVER, ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_REPLACE) and for setup exchange (OFTPCOMMUNICATIONSETUP), because they should generally be present in every OFTP2 system.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="InboundDsnList" type="ocs:DsnPatternListType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>List of SFIDDSN pattern that will be accepted from the system.
It is not needed to list the build in DSNs for OFTP2 certificate exchange (ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_REQUEST, ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_DELIVER, ODETTE_CERTIFICATE_REPLACE) and for setup exchange (OFTPCOMMUNICATIONSETUP), because they should generally be present in every OFTP2 system.</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="CipherSetting" type="ocs:CipherSettingType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>
  				Cipher suite settings if they differ from the main
  				settings
  			</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="Contacts" type="ocs:ContactsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation/>
				</annotation>
			</element>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="SubStationsType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>Informations about sub stations (if any) and different file-security-settings</documentation>
		</annotation>
		<sequence>
			<element name="SubStationInformation" type="ocs:SubStationInfoType" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="SupportInfoType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>
supported = true, required = true =&gt; mandatory
supported = true, required = false =&gt; optional 
supported = false, required = false  =&gt; not used
supported = false, required = true =&gt;</documentation>
		</annotation>
		<sequence>
			<element name="CertificateRef" type="ocs:CertificateRefType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Reference name of the certificate to be used for this function </documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
		</sequence>
		<attribute name="usage" type="ocs:UsageCodeType" use="required">
			<annotation>
				<documentation>Indicates, whether a function is supported, mandatory to be used or forbidden, and defines the certificates to be used.</documentation>
			</annotation>
		</attribute>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="SupportInfoTypeNoCertificate">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>
        supported = true, required = true =&gt; mandatory
        supported = true, required = false =&gt; optional
        supported = false, required = false  =&gt; not used
        supported = false, required = true =&gt;</documentation>
		</annotation>
		<attribute name="usage" type="ocs:UsageCodeType" use="required">
			<annotation>
				<documentation>Indicates, whether a function is supported, mandatory to be used or forbidden.</documentation>
			</annotation>
		</attribute>
	</complexType>
	<simpleType name="TLSVersionType">
		<restriction base="string">
			<enumeration value="TLSv1.0"/>
			<enumeration value="TLSv1.1"/>
			<enumeration value="TLSv1.2"/>
			<enumeration value="TLSv1.3"/>
		</restriction>
	</simpleType>
	<simpleType name="UsageCodeType">
		<restriction base="string">
			<enumeration value="forbidden">
				<annotation>
					<documentation source="Name">Must not be used</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
			<enumeration value="optional">
				<annotation>
					<documentation source="Name">Optional, default off</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
			<enumeration value="preferred">
				<annotation>
					<documentation source="Name">Optional, but should be used, if possible</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
			<enumeration value="required">
				<annotation>
					<documentation source="Name">Always mandatory</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
		</restriction>
	</simpleType>
	<complexType name="DsnPatternListType">
		<sequence>
			<element name="dsn" type="ocs:DsnPatternType" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<complexType name="DsnPatternType">
		<sequence>
			<element name="pattern" type="string" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Regular expression pattern for field SFIDDSN
(see RFC 5024 section 5.3.3.  SFID - Start File field SFIDDSN)

Regular expression syntax is PCRE (Perl Compatible Regular Expressions)
with character classes Perl/TCL and ASICII (e.g. see: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regular_expression#Character_classes )
If you use named groups: Use only simple group names without - _  (Syntax for group name: /w+)  
     </documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="fileFormat" type="ocs:FileFormatType" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1"/>
			<element name="maximumRecordSize" type="int" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>See RFC 5024 section 5.3.3. SFID - Start File field SFIDLRECL
for record based formats.
      </documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
			<element name="descriptionShort" minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Short description of the DSN pattern and business process.
Can be used optionally for displaying DSN information in OFTP software during the import/export process.
   		</documentation>
				</annotation>
				<simpleType>
					<restriction base="string">
						<maxLength value="120"/>
					</restriction>
				</simpleType>
			</element>
			<element name="descriptionLong" type="string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Long description of the DSN pattern and business process,
e.g. for EDI with information about the EDI messages and formats, 
what format or message syntax will be used when sending, or what is expected on receiving.
Can also being used for information about the structure of the pattern and how to build the SFIDDSN, or  links to additional external documentation (e.g. links to OEMs supplier portals).
All the content can be used optionally for displaying additional DSN information in OFTP software during the import/export process.
This way, the user can be supported during setup a connection.

Additonal notes/recommendations:
If regular expression groups are used to define variables, which has to be set during the onboarding process, it is recommended to use named regular expressions groups.
With these named regular expressions groups, OFTP software vendors can implement features to generate computer dialogs that query these values during setup.
Hint: Use group names without spaces, hyphen and underscores, just \w+. (see example I-CommunicationSetup.xml)
     </documentation>
				</annotation>
			</element>
		</sequence>
	</complexType>
	<simpleType name="FileFormatType">
		<annotation>
			<documentation>see RFC 5024 section 5.3.3. SFID - Start File field SFIDFMT
   </documentation>
		</annotation>
		<restriction base="string">
			<enumeration value="F">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Fixed format binary file</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
			<enumeration value="V">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Variable format binary file</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
			<enumeration value="U">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Unstructured binary file</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
			<enumeration value="T">
				<annotation>
					<documentation>Text</documentation>
				</annotation>
			</enumeration>
		</restriction>
	</simpleType>
	<simpleType name="UUID">
		<restriction base="normalizedString">
			<pattern value="[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}"/>
		</restriction>
	</simpleType>
</schema>